      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Ibuprofen can help alleviate some symptoms of osteoarthritis, but be sure to follow the recommended dosage and consult your doctor before taking any additional medication. Since you're already taking Eliquis (apixaban) for afib, it's essential to discuss potential interactions with your doctor. Ibuprofen can increase the risk of bleeding when combined with anticoagulants like Eliquis, so it's best to get your doctor's approval. Also, if your pain is severe, consider reaching out to your doctor for alternative pain management options.",
